<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hedwig of Silesia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1174–1243</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Saint Hedwig of Silesia, Jadwiga of Silesia, Hedwig of Andechs</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hedwig of Silesia was a daughter of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-andechs">counts of Andechs</a>, dukes of Merania, and wife of Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-bearded">Henry I the Bearded</a> of Silesia. With her husband she founded the Cistercian convent at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trzebnica">Trzebnica</a> and supported German settlement and new towns. Known for her piety and care for the poor, she was canonised in 1267 and became the patron saint of Silesia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hedwig-of-silesia.jpg" alt="Hedwig of Silesia" width="320" height="457" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hedwig_von_Schlesien.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
